# Build output. Nothing in this directory is ever committed.
#
# The DLLs here are produced from src/ with CMake, and they belong in a GitHub release as an
# attached archive rather than in the history: a binary in a commit outlives the source it was
# built from, and nobody can tell afterwards which revision produced it.
#
# This file is the only thing in here that git tracks, so the directory survives a clone and says
# what it is for.
#
# To fill it:
#     cmake -S . -B build -A Win32
#     cmake --build build --config Release
#     ctest --test-dir build -C Release
#     copy build\dist\ here without obi_dedicated.exe, plus everything in dist\:
#     engine_fixes.ini, characters.ini, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and the licence texts it
#     names, dxwrapper-License.txt, hacl-License.txt and mbedtls-License.txt
#
# obi_dedicated.exe is the dedicated server. The build makes it, but it is not part of a patch
# release. Anything else in build\dist that the build did not write, such as a file copied in by
# hand for an earlier test, does not belong in the release either; a fresh build directory has
# none.
#
# build\dist is already laid out the way an installation is: dinput.dll beside the executable,
# mods\ and tools\ under it. tools\ holds the standalone scripts, which have no build step and are
# copied there by CMake rather than by hand, because a release assembled partly automatically and
# partly by remembering a folder is one that eventually ships without it.

*
!.gitignore

